ORY|FIRST_END_UNPROVED|SAVINGS_RESIDUALS_NOT_CLOSED|LATER_SOURCE_SEARCH_NOT_RECORDED","claim_present":"no","claim_record_errors":"","decision_origin":"inherited_legacy_v2","exhausted_steps":"","instrument_id":"EO:8960","provisional_status":"no","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"open","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"n/a","step_original_text":"done","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"6","steps_done":"2"},"readiness_blockers":[],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"EXECUTIVE ORDER\nAmending  E xecutive  O rder N o. 8546 of \nSeptember  24, 1940, C reating  the  D e­\nfense  C ommunications  B oard and D e­\nfining  I ts F unctions  and D uties\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me \nas President of the United States, and by \nthe Communications Act of 1934 (48 Stat. \n1064), as amended, it is ordered that Ex­\necutive Order No. 85461  of September 24, \n1940, creating the Defense Communica­\ntions Board and defining its functions \nand duties, be, and it is hereby, amended \nby substituting for the words “Assistant \nSecretary of the Treasury in Charge of \nthe Coast Guard”, wherever they appear \nin the said order, the words “Assistant \nSecretary of the Treasury in Charge of \nTreasury Enforcement Activities” .\nF r a n k l in D  Ro o sevelt \nT h e W h it e H o u s e,\nDecember 6, 1941.\n[No. 8960]\n[F. R. Doc. 41-9236; Filed, December 9, 1941;  \n9:21 a. m.]","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-8960-4a6c7ccee6.txt","sha256":"8512d62c810ede45e6f443461dac29c3898ba24d04f19a96d9240d2d71b0cc4c","source":{"line":638,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"0c858f7bd09fa5878e1267b0ee833654d30da2a3062b4043e85b654b8862682b"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:8960\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1941-12-10/pdf/FR-1941-12-10.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 4a6c7ccee6d9d64e8c2826390a4e480f0ac1e3194077a4667fe0ab7cd93fe405\nLocation: 6 FR 6325, PDF pages 5-5 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 5 of 26 ===\n6325FEDERAL REGISTER, Wednesday, December 10, 1941\nStates or the political processes and pub­\nlic opinions thereof; and to comply \nstrictly with the regulations which are \nhereby or which may be from time to \ntime promulgated by the President.\nAll alien enemies shall be liable to re­\nstraint, or to give security, or to remove \nand depart from the United States in the \nmanner prescribed by Sections 23 and 24 \nof Title 50 of the United States Code, \nand as prescribed in the regulations duly \npromulgated by the President.\nDuties and Authority of the Attorney\nGeneral and the Secretary of War\nAnd, pursuant to the authority vested \nin me, I hereby charge the Attorney \nGeneral with the duty of executing all \nthe regulations hereinafter prescribed \nregarding the conduct of alien enemies \nwithin continental United States, Puerto \nRico, the Virgin Islands and Alaska, and \nthe Secretary of War with the duty of \nexecuting the regulations which are \nhereinafter prescribed and which may be \nhereafter ado","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_8960.txt","sha256":"d15961f26718a1e55fb1246367eaaf6656915cd20055fc5cb1b3d3ab0c8764b8","source":{"line":186,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"51ddd991878ef37a9982eb6a4d440ed1b29ae73e7ddfd278a901ccfd045eeb97"}}]}
